[gd_scene load_steps=79 format=3]

; BT-10 — the TV room. PORTED from C:/repos/mp-foundation scenes/game/world/rooms/Den.tscn
; (no shared git history, so a file port and not a cherry-pick). The Den's own 5.4 x 5.4 x 2.6
; shell is DISCARDED and BT-0's 12 x 12 x 4 shell is kept, because BubbleTestLayout is the
; layout authority and BubbleTestLayoutTests guards it; the Den's CONTENTS are what was ported,
; re-spaced to the larger room. The seven picture frames keep their exact rotation matrices —
; the intent is in the angles.
;
; DIRECTED 2026-08-28 (/direct, THRILL-BIBLE Part II, "The TV that is a doorway"). Four rulings
; are physically visible in this file and must not be undone without re-directing:
;   1. NO SectionLabel. The stub this replaced carried one reading "TV ROOM". A name is an
;      all-clear — it tells the player the game meant this, and being told resolves the
;      ambiguity the room runs on. (UI-1, 2026-08-28: the billboarded SectionLabel came out of
;      the other five sections too, on Talon's ruling. This room's ruling is unchanged and now
;      agrees with the rest of the test rather than standing alone against it.)
;   2. The lamp DOES NOT FLICKER. A flicker is a startle shape used as a build (THRILL 8.2), it
;      becomes a reliable telegraph the second time (8.3), and it is an animate thing in a room
;      whose whole charge is that nothing is animate. The room's entire animation budget is the
;      return TV's static, which was already moving before the player arrived.
;   3. The return TV is BEHIND the arrival point, not in front of it. A player arrives at local
;      (0, 0.4, 3) facing -Z (the entrance TVs are oriented so the approach heading is -Z, and a
;      teleport resets MoveState.Yaw to 0, which is also -Z), so they land looking at the couch,
;      the carpet and the crooked frames, and must turn to find the way out. Fairness bound
;      (THRILL 7.1, and this room is sealed with nothing to rescue a stuck player): turning is
;      the cost, SEARCHING IS NOT — the TV is unmissable the instant they turn.
;   4. The frames stay crooked AND STAY EMPTY. mp-foundation's ElsewhereRoom is the inverse of
;      this room by design (straight, empty, too-much-order); Sail ports the den, so Sail gets
;      the den's half and must not import the other half's register on top. A picture inside a
;      frame is exposition — this room explains nothing about who lived here.
;
; RoomTv authors its Screen / ScreenGlowPool / ScreenTrigger here rather than letting TvPortal
; build them at _Ready, because BubbleTestSelfTest.CheckBake counts a section's PACKED nodes
; against its LIVE ones and fails on any difference. TvPortal adopts all three when present.

