; ---- RoomF's drawing and its lamp (FRAME-1, Talon 2026-09-04) --------------------------------
; Talon: "the TV in the lake, the room that it takes you ... it's nothing. It's nothing special ...
; if you know about it and you find it, you should be rewarded with something sort of fantastic.
; ... maybe there is a picture frame and or like a drawing on the wall ... Can you put if I gave
; you a drawing to put on the wall a PNG with transparency?"  And, on size: "Please made it large
; enough to at least the player can see it."
;
; THE DRAWING IS resources/SecretRoomPicture.png - his own crayon "fwends": four televisions and
; four figures on a torn sheet of paper with a strip of masking tape at the top. 1388 x 1053, RGBA,
; 24.1% of it fully transparent. BubbleTestLayout.SecretPictureImagePath is the constant;
; BubbleTestWorld.SetUpSecretPicture loads it behind a ResourceLoader.Exists guard, refits the
; Canvas below to the image's own aspect inside SecretPictureMountM, and shows it. Swap the PNG and
; nothing here changes; delete it and the wall goes back to a lit, empty mount, not to an error.
;
; NO PICTURE FRAME, and the artwork is the reason. The alpha IS the shape - the paper draws its own
; torn edge and its own tape - so a moulding would box a thing that already has an edge and would
; hide the transparency the request was about. It hangs as a sheet taped to the wall.
;
; NOT the Den's crooked frames either. This file's header ruling 4 ("the frames stay crooked AND
; STAY EMPTY ... A picture inside a frame is exposition") governs the Den, whose frames are
; untouched. RoomF is not a Den, was authored as its deliberate inverse, and Talon has now asked
; for exactly one drawing in exactly this room.
;
; ART-BIBLE: the sheet is an EVENT, not landscape (2.4) - that is what licenses a high-value
; surface against a wall deliberately below the landscape value floor. It is RoomF's ONE hero
; accent (2.3, max two). Its lamp is warm against a cool room - reconciliation C1's intended
; composition, and LEVEL-BIBLE 2.2's counter-signal that this is a reward and not a threat. The
; lamp casts NO SHADOW (7 amendment item 3, closed 2026-08-07). The image is the game's SECOND
; texture and 4.4's "there is no second texture" is knowingly spent on it; see FRAME-1's report.

[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="Mat_lamp_F"]
resource_name = "room F picture lamp - dulled brass"
albedo_color = Color(0.55, 0.46, 0.3, 1)
metallic = 0.2
roughness = 0.35

; TRANSPARENCY = 1 is TRANSPARENCY_ALPHA, and it is the whole answer to Talon's question. An
; opaque material would flatten the torn edge and the clear surround into a solid rectangle; alpha
; blend lets the murk wall show through them. albedo_color stays pure white so the drawing's own
; paper and crayon are what show - a tint here would be repainting his art.
[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="Mat_picture_F"]
resource_name = "room F secret drawing - Talon's fwends, alpha respected"
transparency = 1
albedo_color = Color(1, 1, 1, 1)
roughness = 0.9

[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="Mat_rail_F"]
resource_name = "room F mount rail - bleached driftwood"
albedo_color = Color(0.7, 0.66, 0.58, 1)
roughness = 0.85

