; FRAME-1. On the NORTH wall, dead ahead of the arrival point and 9.0 m from it: a teleport resets
; MoveState.Yaw to 0 (-Z), and BubbleTestLayout.RoomArrivalOffset lands the traveller at room-local
; (0, 0.4, 3), so this is the first thing in the frame when the room resolves. It is a reward for
; finding the room, not a second secret - THRILL 7.1's "turning is the cost, SEARCHING IS NOT" read
; forward: here not even the turn is charged.
;
; y = 2.0 is BubbleTestLayout.SecretPictureCentreY. Maximising the sheet under an even margin of
; one AvatarProportions.PlayerCrownM puts its centre at the wall's own mid-height by construction
; (margin/2 + height/2 = TvRoomHeight/2). FRAME-1's packet asked for the avatar's 0.995 m eyeline
; and Talon then asked for it big enough to read from the arrival point; in a 4 m room those are
; arithmetically incompatible (an eyeline-centred sheet caps at 1.99 m tall) and size won. The
; avatar still sets the size, through the margin. BubbleTestSelfTest.CheckSecretPicture reads this
; node's live local Y back and fails if it ever disagrees with the constant.
;
; z = -6.0 is the north wall's inner face (WallNorth sits at -6.25, 0.5 thick). Nothing is behind
; the sheet but the wall, so the transparent surround and the torn edge show the murk through.
[node name="SecretPicture" type="Node3D" parent="RoomF"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 2.0, -6.0)

; HIDDEN IN THE FILE, SHOWN BY THE GUARD, and that is the empty state. Talon's PNG ships, so this
; is normally visible within a frame of load; delete or rename the file and the wall goes back to a
; lit, empty mount rather than to a magenta error texture or a console error.
[node name="Canvas" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="RoomF/SecretPicture" groups=["no_collider"]]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0.02)
visible = false
material_override = SubResource("Mat_picture_F")
mesh = SubResource("QuadMesh_picture_F")

; THE EMPTY STATE'S ANCHOR, and the one piece of mounting hardware this wall carries. A batten
; 0.14 m above the paper's top edge: it does not box the drawing, does not overlap it and hides
; none of its alpha, which is what a moulding around a sheet that draws its own torn edge and its
; own tape would have done. What it does is make the wall read as a place a drawing HANGS when
; there is no drawing on it - with the PNG deleted the room shows a lit rail under a lit lamp
; rather than a lamp aimed at nothing, which is the difference between a designed empty state and
; something that looks broken. Measured: without it the empty capture is a bare lit oval on a
; wall (docs/qa/FRAME-1's first pass).
[node name="MountRail" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="RoomF/SecretPicture" groups=["no_collider"]]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1.52, 0.03)
material_override = SubResource("Mat_rail_F")
mesh = SubResource("BoxMesh_rail_F")

[node name="LampDrop" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="RoomF/SecretPicture" groups=["no_collider"]]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1.805, 3.0)
material_override = SubResource("Mat_lamp_F")
mesh = SubResource("BoxMesh_lampdrop_F")

[node name="LampHood" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="RoomF/SecretPicture" groups=["no_collider"]]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1.53, 3.0)
material_override = SubResource("Mat_lamp_F")
mesh = SubResource("BoxMesh_lamphood_F")

; THE ONLY LIGHT THIS PACKET ADDS, and it lights the drawing and nothing else. The room's own
; RoomFill omni below is untouched, no WorldEnvironment is added (EGG-1's recorded trap), and
; shadows stay off (ART-BIBLE 7 amendment item 3, closed 2026-08-07).
;
; CEILING-MOUNTED, 3.0 m out from the wall, and that is measured rather than styled. A lamp on a
; short bracket above the sheet cannot light 2.76 m of paper: at 0.8 m out the incidence across the
; drawing runs 0.91 at the top against 0.17 at the bottom - top clipped, bottom black. From
; (0, 1.50, 3.00) sheet-local it runs 1.00 to 0.72 down the height and never below 0.66 at the far
; corners, which is a wash rather than a hotspot.
;
; The basis is written columns-as-axes per Godot's .tscn convention: -Z, the direction a
; SpotLight3D emits along, comes out (0, -0.44962, -0.89325), the unit vector from (0, 1.50, 3.00)
; to the sheet's centre at (0, 0, 0.02). 44 degrees contains the far bottom corner (29.1 degrees
; off axis) and the top corners (39.0) with margin; spot_range 6.5 clears the 4.53 m to the
; furthest corner.
[node name="PictureLight" type="SpotLight3D" parent="RoomF/SecretPicture"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 0.89325, 0.44962, 0, -0.44962, 0.89325, 0, 1.5, 3.0)
light_color = Color(1, 0.93, 0.84, 1)
light_energy = 5.0
shadow_enabled = false
spot_range = 6.5
spot_angle = 44.0
spot_angle_attenuation = 1.0

