; ---- BUBBLE-1: bubbles in the rooms the televisions take you to -------------------------------
; Talon, 2026-09-04, off a live playtest: "there are not any bubbles at all in most of the TV
; areas ... I would like some bubbles to be moved from the outside to inside of some of these."
; He was right and the file proves it: all three of this section's shipped bubbles sat in the Den
; (the Bubbles node at the scene root), and RoomB, C, D, E and F had none between them.
;
; Three each into RoomB, RoomC, RoomD and RoomF. TvRoomBubbles goes 3 -> 15.
;
; ROOM E DELIBERATELY GETS NONE, and it is a reachability fact rather than a taste.
; BubbleTestWorld.DestinationFor overrides HiddenTv -- RoomE's only television -- to the puffin
; lab's Arrival whenever PuffinLab.tscn is in the build, which is every shipped build. So nothing
; goes to RoomE; it keeps its way out and no way in. A bubble there would be one the player can
; never reach, which is what turns "collect all the bubbles" into a lie. The lab is RoomE's
; replacement and the lab is where those bubbles went instead (PuffinLabBubbles = 10). RoomE
; having no route while the lab is present is EGG-2's finding, not this packet's to fix.
;
; EVERY POSITION BELOW IS INSIDE ITS ROOM'S SEALED BOX. The rooms do not touch -- there is no
; floor and no geometry at all in the void between them -- so a bubble authored outside a room's
; interior would be counted and uncollectable at once. Interior half-extents, room-local:
; RoomB x +/-5, RoomC x +/-7, RoomD x +/-6, RoomF x +/-5; all four z +/-6, floor top y = 0,
; ceiling underside y = 4 except RoomD's, which is y = 3.
;
; TWO KEEP-OUTS THAT ARE NOT IN THE COLLIDERS, so measuring against the physics space alone is
; not enough here:
;   - the couch's RENDERED mesh is 2.89 x 1.91 x 2.20 m, over three times its 1.8 x 0.8 x 0.9
;     collision hull, and 149 of its vertices sit above y = 1.0 across the whole footprint. The
;     Den's shipped Bubble_Tv_01 at (0, 1.4, -1.6) is inside that upper mass -- it clears the hull
;     by 0.60 m and clears the visual by nothing. That placement is left alone (it is shipped, and
;     the bubble is visible and poppable) but it is NOT copied into the other four rooms;
;   - RoomTv/ScreenTrigger is the teleport OUT, a 0.8 x 1.2 x 0.45 box at local (0, 0.55, 4.78).
;     A bubble that makes the player walk into it teleports them instead of paying them, so every
;     position below stays clear of x in [-1.2, 1.2] while z > 3.7.
; Nothing else in these rooms has a collider: the picture frames, the light stands and the silt
; drifts are all uncollided visuals, so their RENDERED boxes are what the clearances are against.

[node name="Bubbles" type="Node3D" parent="RoomB"]

; North-east floor, 2.4 m off the east wall and 2.45 m short of the picture-frame plane.
[node name="Bubble_TvB_01" parent="RoomB/Bubbles" instance=ExtResource("8_bubble")]
position = Vector3(2.6, 1.2, -3.2)

; West side. The couch's x-band runs -3.44..-0.56, so the whole 2.02 m clearance is in z.
[node name="Bubble_TvB_02" parent="RoomB/Bubbles" instance=ExtResource("8_bubble")]
position = Vector3(-3.4, 1.2, 1.6)

; South-east floor. MOVED HERE from (-3.2, 1.1, 4.4), which the reach check caught: that put it
; 0.45 m from GoldCube_RoomB_0 at room-local (-3.0, 4.0), so the straight walk from the arrival
; point went through the crate. The cube is a Crate.tscn body authored into BubbleTest.tscn's
; Props node -- carryable, and therefore not a wall, but a bubble standing on top of one is not a
; placement anybody chose. 4.8 m from the cube here, 1.7 m off the south wall, and clear of the
; screen trigger's x band by 0.6 m.
[node name="Bubble_TvB_03" parent="RoomB/Bubbles" instance=ExtResource("8_bubble")]
position = Vector3(1.8, 1.1, 4.3)

[node name="Bubbles" type="Node3D" parent="RoomC"]

; RoomC is the big room (14 x 12) and its whole west half holds nothing but frames on the north
; wall, so this one is in genuinely open floor -- nothing within 7 m but the wall behind it.
[node name="Bubble_TvC_01" parent="RoomC/Bubbles" instance=ExtResource("8_bubble")]
position = Vector3(-5.0, 1.2, -2.0)

; East side, 1.5 m off the wall and 2.0 m from the couch's near corner.
[node name="Bubble_TvC_02" parent="RoomC/Bubbles" instance=ExtResource("8_bubble")]
position = Vector3(5.5, 1.2, 1.5)

; The corridor between the couch's back (z = -2.78) and the frame fronts (z = -5.65): 1.42 m and
; 1.48 m. The one placement in this room that has to be walked to rather than seen from arrival.
[node name="Bubble_TvC_03" parent="RoomC/Bubbles" instance=ExtResource("8_bubble")]
position = Vector3(2.0, 1.3, -4.2)

[node name="Bubbles" type="Node3D" parent="RoomD"]

; RoomD's ceiling is 3 m rather than 4, so nothing here goes above y = 1.4: at 1.4 the visual
; sphere plus its 0.15 m bob tops out at 2.0, a metre clear of the slab.
[node name="Bubble_TvD_01" parent="RoomD/Bubbles" instance=ExtResource("8_bubble")]
position = Vector3(-4.0, 1.2, 0.5)

; East side. MOVED HERE from the north-east corner pocket at (4.6, 1.2, -4.3), which cleared the
; reach check but sat 0.92 m from GoldCube_RoomD_0 at room-local (4.0, -5.0) -- the same crowding
; the RoomB bubble above was caught for, close enough to be worth not shipping twice. 2.7 m from
; the cube here, 1.0 m off the east wall, 4.1 m from the couch.
[node name="Bubble_TvD_02" parent="RoomD/Bubbles" instance=ExtResource("8_bubble")]
position = Vector3(5.0, 1.2, -2.5)

; South-west, behind the arriving player: yaw resets to 0 on a teleport so this one is at their
; back, and turning is the cost (THRILL 7.1, the same rule the room's arrival geometry follows).
[node name="Bubble_TvD_03" parent="RoomD/Bubbles" instance=ExtResource("8_bubble")]
position = Vector3(-3.0, 1.4, 3.5)

[node name="Bubbles" type="Node3D" parent="RoomF"]

; THE DEEP ROOM, and it is deliberately the one room where nothing is hidden. RoomF has no couch,
; no frames and no lamp -- a silt floor under a lit water ceiling -- and the only things in it are
; three knee-high stones (0.5 m) and three 9 cm silt decals. Above y = 0.5 the room is empty, so
; there is nothing to tuck a bubble behind and no pretending otherwise. All three hang in the open.
; Dead centre of the murk: 3.05 m from Stone0, 2.8 m from Stone2, over 4.5 m from every wall.
[node name="Bubble_TvF_01" parent="RoomF/Bubbles" instance=ExtResource("8_bubble")]
position = Vector3(0.0, 1.2, -1.5)

; North-west, over SiltDrift2 -- the decal is 9 cm of floor, so it reads as "above the drift"
; without anything being in the way.
[node name="Bubble_TvF_02" parent="RoomF/Bubbles" instance=ExtResource("8_bubble")]
position = Vector3(-3.2, 1.2, -4.0)

; South-east, 1.77 m clear of the screen trigger and 2.05 m from the cabinet: the one spot in this
; room with a lit object to read against, which is the whole of what makes it findable.
[node name="Bubble_TvF_03" parent="RoomF/Bubbles" instance=ExtResource("8_bubble")]
position = Vector3(2.0, 1.3, 3.8)


; ================================================================================================
; ROOFTOP-1 (2026-09-05) - RoomG, THE SKY DECK. The seventh television's destination, and the only
; "room" in this section with no walls, no ceiling, no couch and no lamp.
;
; Talon: "all it did was take the player to like you're right like an impossibly high angle and on
; this angle, there is the very last bubble the 100 bubble and maybe it's on like a diving board so
; it's funny and the player can jump and catch the bubble ... and then so then they get to fall and
; they get to see the whole map from a very top of the whole world? This would be fun, right?"
;
; WHY IT IS IN THIS FILE AT ALL, 220 m above the section it belongs to. TvPortalSelfTest finds
; every route's way out at the hard path "TvRoom/<ReturnTvPath>", so a destination outside this
; section node has no way back the shipped test can see - and a room a player can enter and not
; leave is the one failure this level treats as unrecoverable. The TV room is already the section
; that is nowhere in the world (its footprint overlaps everything and it is exempted by name from
; three separate checks); a room 200 m UP is the same kind of nowhere as a room 20 m down. It is
; also directly over the hub, which is what makes the fall land on the flattest 80 x 80 m in the
; level. BubbleTestLayout.SkyDeckRoomCentre carries the whole argument and the arithmetic.
;
; THE ONE CONSTANT THIS ROOM COST: MaxHeightOf(TvRoom) had to split off TvRoomHeight, because
; CheckFootprints bounds a section's meshes at anchor + MaxHeightOf + 0.5 and this room is 220 m
; up. TvRoomHeight itself did NOT move - it is the sealed box's height and four other things read
; it. See BubbleTestLayout.TvRoomCeilingM.
;
; NOTHING HERE IS ANIMATED, LIT OR SEQUENCED. No spring on the board, no camera move, no effect on
; the bubble. The beat is a plank over a 200 m drop; restraint is the direction and the view is
; doing the work.
[node name="RoomG" type="Node3D" parent="."]
position = Vector3(0.0, 220.0, 0.0)

; The deck: 14 x 14 m, top face at room-local 0 (world y = 200). Big enough to arrive, turn, walk
; to the board and walk to the way out; small enough that there is an edge in sight on every side.
; No rail, deliberately - a rail on a diving platform is a rail against the only thing this place
; is for.
[node name="Deck" type="Node3D" parent="RoomG"]
position = Vector3(0, -0.25, 0)

[node name="Mesh" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="RoomG/Deck"]
material_override = SubResource("Mat_deck_G")
mesh = SubResource("BoxMesh_deck_G")

[node name="Body" type="StaticBody3D" parent="RoomG/Deck"]

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="RoomG/Deck/Body"]
shape = SubResource("BoxShape3D_deck_G")

; The board's mount, touching the deck's north face and hanging under the plank's root. It is what
; makes the silhouette read as a diving board rather than as a plank somebody left out: from the
; deck you see a stand, and from underneath you see the cantilever.
[node name="BoardMount" type="Node3D" parent="RoomG"]
position = Vector3(0, -0.37, -7.7)

[node name="Mesh" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="RoomG/BoardMount"]
material_override = SubResource("Mat_deck_G")
mesh = SubResource("BoxMesh_fulcrum_G")

[node name="Body" type="StaticBody3D" parent="RoomG/BoardMount"]

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="RoomG/BoardMount/Body"]
shape = SubResource("BoxShape3D_fulcrum_G")

; The board: 1.2 x 10 m, leaving the deck's north edge (z = -7) and ending at z = -17
; (BubbleTestLayout.DivingBoardTipZ). ITS TOP IS FLUSH WITH THE DECK - the walk out has to be a
; walk. A plank standing proud would be a step at the root of a board over a 200 m drop, and this
; game has no automatic step-up: a lip there is a stumble the player pays for with the whole ride.
; A teleport resets yaw to 0 (-Z), so a player arriving at RoomArrivalOffset is already looking
; straight down it with the way out behind them - the same rule every other room in this file
; follows, and here it aims the arrival at the joke.
[node name="Board" type="Node3D" parent="RoomG"]
position = Vector3(0, -0.06, -12.0)

[node name="Mesh" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="RoomG/Board"]
material_override = SubResource("Mat_board_G")
mesh = SubResource("BoxMesh_board_G")

[node name="Body" type="StaticBody3D" parent="RoomG/Board"]

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="RoomG/Board/Body"]
shape = SubResource("BoxShape3D_board_G")

; THE HUNDREDTH BUBBLE IS NOT IN THIS FILE. It is Bubble_Seam_02 in Hub.tscn, RELOCATED rather
; than added: ids are the index of an ordinal node-path sort, so moving the node here would
; renumber the level, and editing its position leaves it as id 48. See
; BubbleTestLayout.SkyBubblePos, and Hub.tscn's own note where it now hangs.

; The way out, 2.2 m south of where a traveller lands - the same geometry as every other room, so
; the rule is one rule and not seven. It returns to cyan's plate rather than to the lab roof,
; because a room's way out must leave the room and the roof is under grade; see
; BubbleTestLayout.RooftopTvReturn.
[node name="RoomTv" type="Node3D" parent="RoomG"]
